      <div type="clause" n="11">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Grith">Grið</ref> 11</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="11" corresp="#wit-g-b"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="†" target="#Grith_11.lnote.oe.dagger"/><pb n="471" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gyf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Grith_11.lnote.oe.1"/> hwa cynges mundbrice elles gewyrce, gebete þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> mid V pundum on Engla lage, arceb<hi rend="italic">iscopes</hi> ⁊ æþelinges mundbrice<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Grith_11.lnote.oe.2"/> mid þri<hi rend="italic">m</hi> pundum, oðres biscpæs<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Grith_11.lnote.oe.3"/> ⁊ ealdormannes mid II pundum.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" n="11" corresp="#wit-g-b"><pb n="24" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And gyf hwa cynges mundbrice elles gewyrce, gebete þæt mid V pundum on Engla lage, arcebiscopes and æþelinges mundbrice mid þrim pundum; oðres biscpæs and ealdormannes mid II pundum.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="471" ed="#liebermann"/>Und wenn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Grith_11.lnote.de.1"/> einer anderweitig Verletzung königlicher Schutzgewalt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Grith_11.lnote.de.2"/> verübt, büsse er dies im Engländer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="a" target="#Grith_11.lnote.de1.a"/>-Recht mit 5 Pfund, Verletzung der Schutzgewalt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#Grith_11.lnote.de1.star"/> eines Erzbischofs und [= oder<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Grith_11.lnote.de.3"/>] eines Prinzen mit 3 Pfund, die eines anderen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#Grith_11.lnote.de1.star-2"/> Bischofs und [= oder] eines Ealdorman mit 2 Pfund.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And if anyone otherwise commits breach of the king's protection, let him atone for it under English law with 5 pounds; breach of the protection of an archbishop and [= or] of a prince with 3 pounds; that of another bishop and [= or] of an ealdorman with 2 pounds.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-b"><pb n="25" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And if anyone otherwise violates the king’s protection, he is to compensate for that with five pounds according to English law; violation of an archbishop’s and nobleman’s protection with three pounds; another bishop’s and ealdorman’s with two pounds.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="471"><ref target="clause:IICn_58">II Cn 58–58.2</ref>; <ref target="clause:Af_3">Af 3</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">II Cn. 58—58, 2 | *Af 3</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="353"><label>closer to original</label> <ref target="clause:Af_3">Af 3</ref> <quote>the form of the equivalent law in Grið 11 is in some ways closer to Alfred's original</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="353"><label>equivalent</label> <ref target="clause:IICn_58">II Cn 58–58.2</ref> <quote>As regards II Cn 58 – 58:2 above, note that the form of the equivalent law in Grið 11 is in some ways closer to Alfred's original</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">‘English law’ here means the law of the southern English (9), Liebermann notes. Liebermann compares II Cn 58–58.2 and Af 3.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Grith_11.lnote.oe.dagger" n="†" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">471</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">11 <hi rend="italic">f. benutzt in</hi> Inst. Cn. 56, 2. 57, <hi rend="italic">o. S.</hi> 470†</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">11 f. used in Inst. Cn. 56, 2. 57, above p. 470†</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Grith_11.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">471</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">i <hi rend="italic">statt</hi> y <hi rend="italic">Tho.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">i instead of y Tho.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Grith_11.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">471</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-bryce <hi rend="italic">Wi. Tho.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-bryce Wi. Tho.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Grith_11.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">471</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">biscopes <hi rend="italic">Wi. Tho., aber vgl.</hi> 12 <hi rend="italic">und VI Atr.</hi> 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">biscopes Wi. Tho., but cf. 12 and VI Atr. 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Grith_11.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">266</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Kompiliert aus mehreren Sätzen. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Königsschutz 5</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Compiled from several sentences. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Königsschutz 5</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Grith_11.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">266</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Ebd</hi>. Schutz 3. 14. Modernisierend ersetzt Verf. <hi rend="italic">borg</hi> durch <hi rend="italic">mund</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Ibid.</hi> Schutz 3. 14. Modernizing, the author replaces <hi rend="italic">borg</hi> by <hi rend="italic">mund</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Grith_11.lnote.de1.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">471</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">= Südengländer 9</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">= South English 9</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Grith_11.lnote.de1.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">471</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">auch</hi> 14—18 <hi rend="italic">sind particular Nordenglisch</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">14—18 too are specifically Northern English</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Grith_11.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">266</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Wb: and</hi> 2; auch <hi rend="italic">u</hi>. 17. Vielleicht <hi rend="italic">ł</hi> verlesen für ⁊</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Wb: and</hi> 2; also <hi rend="italic">below</hi> 17. Perhaps <hi rend="italic">ł</hi> misread for ⁊</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Grith_11.lnote.de1.star-2" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">471</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">auch</hi> 14—18 <hi rend="italic">sind particular Nordenglisch</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">14—18 too are specifically Northern English</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
